Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:58:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Scotch 7.0.18 report: every finding re-checked,
 upstream's fixes reviewed

upstream/reports/7.0.18/ is the second column of the tracker, carried
from 7.0.17 (`carry`) and re-audited group by group on v7.0.18:

- 350 findings, plus 25 new defects (PS3-*). Of the 192 review leads,
  7.0.18 fixes 45 completely and 37 partly; 108 are still present.
- Each upstream 7.0.18 commit that touches a finding has our verdict
  (`upstream_fix_review`): 71 reviewed, 32 correct, 32 incomplete, 7 wrong
  (they introduce a crash, hang or wrong output: 18911e4f, ecaf094e,
  22c9c42e, 86559b85, 27f4193c, 858ea2bc, 59c9a31c).
- SEP-13 (threaded bgraphBipartGg nondeterminism) is unchanged and still
  blocks the bump (blocking.json).
- 232 commits rebased on v7.0.18 (upstream took one of ours verbatim; the
  others it made redundant are dropped and partial ones shrunk to what is
  left; 4 duplicates between groups dropped), exported as one series that
  applies with a plain `git am`.
- QA (qa.json): both Gnum sizes, ASan+UBSan, 0 warnings; make check,
  ptcheck and escheck pass with 0 sanitizer reports. Pristine 7.0.18 fails
  check_scotch_arch_build and shows 23-25 UBSan reports in check and 7 in
  ptcheck.

Reproducer kits in upstream/repro/ are updated in place.

