+    "preferred_fix": "A. Typed <SAVE> mid-rule value with a %destructor that restores the context (recommended)"
+   },
+   "severity": "high",
+   "severity_note": "Crash (NULL deref) from any user strategy string with a typo inside a nested parameter; parser_yy.y untouched by 7.0.18.",
+   "ran": "repro/run_strings.sh <libdir> runs all reproducer strings through repro/common/st (pristine: $INFRA/asan/lib, patched: $WORK/build/lib). Pristine 7.0.18: 'r{sep=m{asc=b{:width=3}}}' -> 'parser_yy.y:485:45: runtime error: member access within null pointer of type const struct StratParamTab' then SEGV; 'r{sep=m{asc=(b{width=3}|' -> 'member access within null pointer of type struct Strat'; 'r{sep=m{asc=b{bnd=f,org=f},low=h{:}}}' -> same at :485:45. Patched: 'invalid value for parameter \"asc\" of method \"m\", line 1, column 13', ret=1, no sanitizer output. Mutation fuzz on 7.0.18 (repro/common/fuzz.py, bases regenerated with defstrat on 7.0.18 = repro/common/bases18.txt, 4 default strategies x 600 mutations): pristine 7.0.18 seed 1: 2086/2400 sanitizer hits (1913 leaks parser_yy.y:288, 116+26 NULL deref parser_yy.y:485:72/:45, 3 misaligned Strat* stores parser_yy.y:479, 15 leaks :225, 7 :180, crashes in stratSave library_parser.c:135 / parser.c:212/254); patched series seed 1: 0/2400, seed 2: 0/2400 (repro/common/fuzz18_*.txt). check_strat_seq (32- and 64-bit trees), check_strat_par (mpicc), check_scotch_graph_map, check_scotch_graph_order pass on the patched 32-bit ASan tree (graph_map: 2 pre-existing UBSan 'offset to null pointer' reports bgraph_bipart_ml.c:195 / kgraph_map_ml.c:239, unrelated); 0 warnings on 32- and 64-bit trees; bison 3.8.2 builds the grammar with no conflict, both with make and with CMake after 635741dd (Release configure + 'make scotch', 0 warnings).",
