+  "upstream_change": "22c9c42e Bugfix: make sure hash table does not fill up to capacity [report R. Perry]",
+  "upstream_fix_review": {
+   "commit": "22c9c42e87",
+   "verdict": "wrong",
+   "details": "Right: kgraphMapRbVfloBuild no longer creates slots for zero-load fixed vertices (kgraph_map_rb.c:271-274) and its table is sized from dfixmax = min(vfixnbr, archsize) computed once in kgraphMapRb (:150-160), which bounds its entries; the int shift '1 << (hashsiz + 2)' is gone from both routines; the unused archptr parameter of VfloBuild is dropped. Wrong: kgraphMapRbVfloMerge (:413-415) is now sized from dfixmax ONLY, but it first inserts every domain of the mapping computed on the free vertices (:423-436, mappptr->domnnbr entries, up to the number of parts). 7.0.17 sized it from domnnbr + vflonbr. With fewer than ~domnnbr/4 distinct fixed terminals the table (minimum 8 slots) fills up and the probe loop has no exit: SCOTCH_graphMapFixed/graphPartFixed with 1 fixed vertex and >= 9 parts hangs (default strategy, through kgraphMapMl -> kgraphMapRb), 32/64-bit. The shipped tests only fix 4-12 vertices on small architectures, so they miss it. Minor: 'fariable-sized' typo in the comment at :151. See PS3-G12-1. Independently found by G25 as PS3-G25-1 (same hunk).",
+   "compared_with_ours": "Ours (7.0.17 0003) sized Merge from min(archsize, vfixnbr) + domnnbr and added a regression test (zero-load fixed vertices); his avoids zero-load slots in Build too (nicer: fewer slots) and factors dfixmax once, but drops the domnnbr term and adds no test. Rebased as 0002: keeps his structure, adds mappptr->domnnbr to the Merge bound, and the test now covers both the zero-load case and the single-fixed-vertex case (hangs on pristine 7.0.18 at kgraph_map_rb.c:428)."
