+From c9987509d9a614ce350ca10157d8474b41c21dc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
+Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:55:35 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Bugfix: maintain a consistent ordering for else-less
+ false conditions [report R. Perry]
+
+Since 8609a5cb, a conditional sequential graph ordering strategy with
+no else branch, such as `/(vert>1000)?s;`, applies the default
+ordering method when its condition is false, instead of leaving the
+ordering permutation unset. The distributed graph and mesh ordering
+dispatchers had the same defect: apply `hdgraphOrderSi()` and
+`hmeshOrderSi()` in this case too.
+
+Refs: GRA-06
+---
+ src/libscotch/hdgraph_order_st.c | 2 ++
+ src/libscotch/hmesh_order_st.c   | 2 ++
