+From 5b1e84751ba901baa4be750d5e5a8b054c503437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
+Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:14:19 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Bugfix: do not initialize matching data after a failed
+ coarsening initialization in `dgraphCoarsen()` [report PyScotch]
+
+When `dgraphCoarsenInit()` failed, `dgraphCoarsen()` still called
+`dgraphMatchInit()`, which dereferenced the fine graph pointer that
+had not been set yet, and then called `dgraphMatchExit()` on an
+uninitialized structure and `dgraphCoarsenExit()` on data that
+`dgraphCoarsenInit()` had already freed.
+
+Initialize the matching data only when the coarsening data exists, and
+leave all cleanup to `dgraphCoarsen()`, after all processes have agreed
+on the error.
+
+Refs: PS-DGR-1
+---
+ src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++------------
+ 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c b/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
+index 09540aac..3041197a 100644
+--- a/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
++++ b/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
+@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
