+ \libscotch\ routines) and \texttt{METIS\_\lbt OPTION\_\lbt OBJTYPE}
+-(only for computing the partition cost, as \scotch\ does not try
+-directly to minimize communication volume).
++(which selects whether the edge cut or the communication volume is
++minimized and returned by the \metis\ v5 graph partitioning routines;
++since \scotch\ does not try directly to minimize communication
++volume, the latter is emulated by means of edge loads, as described
++for \texttt{METIS\_\lbt Part\lbt Graph\lbt VKway}).
+ 
+ \end{itemize}
