+From eefe2845526c353d3eec17b17915e30a2128c631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
+Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:15:36 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 156/232] Bugfix: reject fragments without part array in
+ `dmapSave()` [report R. Perry and PyScotch]
+
+A fragment without a part array, as left by a sequential mapping
+strategy that does not compute one, was dereferenced on the root
+process and on the others. Count such fragments in the initial
+reduction, so that all processes give up at once: a non-root process
+that gave up later would leave the root process waiting for its
+fragments.
+
+Refs: DMO-15
